{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794293031,"nonce":"KQ7a1PSuiAqp2PT3VDw0l4qxku8=","title":"ElementStyle is 1856 bytes inline per CSS rule, so the cn stylesheet holds about 4.5 MB","message":"Heap measured on cn_demo (same method as the per-node issue): `Stylesheet::merge` holds one 2.6 MB allocation for `complex_rules` (Vec\u003c(ComplexSelector, ElementStyle)\u003e) and one 1.9 MB table for `class_styles`. `ElementStyle` is 1856 bytes, every property an inline `Option`, while a rule sets a handful. Hello world (theme CSS only) holds 0.6 MB in blinc_css.\n\nA sparse representation (a property-id → value list, or boxing groups such as transitions, filters, 3D, text) would make a rule cost what it sets. `merge` also re-allocates the merged maps on each `add_stylesheet`.","files":null}]}